@startuml outbox-pattern
' Smetana is PlantUML's built-in layout engine, so Graphviz is not needed.
!pragma layout smetana

title Outbox pattern in the Notification App

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 60

component "**EventService**\n(event module)" as EventService #FFF3E0
component "**OutboxWriter**\n(notification module)" as Writer #E8F5E9
component "**Outbox worker**\n(notification module)" as Outbox #E8F5E9
component "**Delivery worker**\n(notification module)" as Delivery #E8F5E9
component "**Email / Slack sender**\n(only logs for now)" as Sender #E8F5E9

database "events" as Events
database "event_outbox" as OutboxTable
database "notification_deliveries" as Deliveries

EventService -down-> Events : 1. save event
EventService -right-> Writer : 2. EventCreated
Writer -down-> OutboxTable : 3. save record\n(PENDING)

OutboxTable -down-> Outbox : 4. claim record
Outbox -down-> Deliveries : 5. one job per\nmatching alert (PENDING)

Deliveries -down-> Delivery : 6. claim job
Delivery -down-> Sender : 7. send

legend bottom
  Steps 1-3: one transaction, so the event and its outbox record are saved together
  Steps 4-5: one transaction; loads the event (EventLookup, event module), finds the enabled alerts
  (AlertLookup, implemented by app), and marks the record PROCESSED
  Steps 6-7: one transaction; loads the event and alert the same way, and marks the job SENT
  Claim: FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
  On failure after claiming: roll back, then mark it FAILED in a second transaction; FAILED is never retried
  After a crash it stays PENDING and is picked up again, so a message can be sent twice (at least once)
end legend

@enduml
